        {
          "kicker": "Bledisloe rematch",
          "heading": "Les Kiss backs Wallabies to return fire after Eden Park defeat",
          "body": "Wallabies head coach Les Kiss has turned his focus to next weekend's Bledisloe Cup rematch in Sydney following a heavy 50-19 defeat to the All Blacks at Eden Park. Australia led 14-17 at half-time after tries from Tom Wright and Harry Wilson, but a dominant second-half display from the hosts extended New Zealand's unbeaten run at the venue to 54 Tests. Kiss remained defiant after suffering his first loss at the helm, telling reporters: \"We’ll go back and we’ll work on what we have to and try and turn the dial in the right areas that can go to Sydney and return fire.\""
        },
        {
